(CHAPTER 1: ACADEMIC REGULATIONS & ATTENDANCE POLICY) Tj
0 -20 Td
/F2 9.5 Tf
(1.1 Minimum Attendance Requirement:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(All undergraduate and postgraduate students are strictly required to maintain a minimum of) Tj
0 -14 Td
(75% attendance in each registered course \(theory lectures, practical lab sessions, and tutorials\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(during the semester in order to be eligible to appear for the End-Semester Final Examination.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -10 Td
(1.2 Attendance Condonation on Medical Grounds:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(In exceptional circumstances involving severe illness, hospitalization, or authorized university) Tj
0 -14 Td
(representation in national sports or academic competitions, attendance condonation may be granted.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(The Dean of Academic Affairs may condone up to a maximum of 10% attendance shortage.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(However, under no circumstances will condonation be approved if student attendance falls below 65%.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Medical certificates must be endorsed by the University Chief Medical Officer within 3 business days.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -10 Td
(1.3 Penalty for Attendance Shortage \(Debarment\):) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Students having attendance below 75% \(or below 65% in condoned medical cases\) shall be officially) Tj
0 -14 Td
(awarded a Withheld / Debarred grade \(Grade W\) in that specific course.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Such debarred students are prohibited from writing the end-semester examination and must repeat) Tj
0 -14 Td
(the entire course in subsequent semesters when the course is offered again.) Tj
0 -14 Td
