(CHAPTER 2: EXAMINATION GUIDELINES & MISCONDUCT REGULATIONS) Tj
0 -20 Td
/F2 9.5 Tf
(2.1 Examination Hall Protocol:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Students must report to the allocated examination hall at least 15 minutes prior to commencement.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Entry is strictly subject to the physical possession of a valid University ID Card and Admit Card.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(No candidate will be allowed entry into the hall after 15 minutes from the scheduled start of the exam.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -10 Td
(2.2 Prohibited Articles in Examination Venues:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(The possession of mobile phones, smartwatches, digital fitness bands, programmable calculators,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(loose papers, or unauthorized study materials inside the examination venue is strictly prohibited.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(All electronic devices must be switched off and deposited at the designated bag rack outside.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -10 Td
(2.3 Classification of Examination Misconduct & Penalties:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Category I \(Minor Misconduct\): Possession of unauthorized handwritten notes or formulas without) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  evidence of active use. Penalty: Immediate cancellation of that specific course examination.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Category II \(Major Misconduct\): Copying from another candidate, passing chits, or utilizing unauthorized) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  digital/smart devices during the exam. Penalty: Cancellation of all registered examinations for that entire) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  semester and award of Fail \(F\) grades across all subjects.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Category III \(Severe Misconduct\): Impersonation, tearing of answer scripts, or verbal/physical intimidation) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  of invigilators. Penalty: Immediate expulsion/rustication from the university for 1 to 2 academic years.) Tj
0 -14 Td
