(CHAPTER 3: GRADING POLICIES & ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE CRITERIA) Tj
0 -20 Td
/F2 9.5 Tf
(3.1 10-Point Relative Grading System:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Academic performance in each registered course is assessed through Continuous Internal Evaluation \(CIE 40%\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(and End-Semester Examination \(ESE 60%\). Final letter grades are assigned on a 10-point scale:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  * Grade O  \(Outstanding\): Grade Point 10.0 \(Marks >= 90%\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  * Grade A+ \(Excellent\): Grade Point 9.0 \(Marks 80% to 89%\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  * Grade A  \(Very Good\): Grade Point 8.0 \(Marks 70% to 79%\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  * Grade B+ \(Good\): Grade Point 7.0 \(Marks 60% to 69%\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  * Grade B  \(Above Average\): Grade Point 6.0 \(Marks 55% to 59%\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  * Grade C  \(Average\): Grade Point 5.0 \(Marks 50% to 54%\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  * Grade P  \(Pass\): Grade Point 4.0 \(Marks 40% to 49%\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  * Grade F  \(Fail\): Grade Point 0.0 \(Marks < 40%\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -10 Td
(3.2 Semester & Cumulative Grade Calculation \(SGPA & CGPA\):) Tj
0 -14 Td
(The Semester Grade Point Average \(SGPA\) is computed as the sum of \(Course Credits * Grade Points\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(divided by the total registered credits for the semester.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(The Cumulative Grade Point Average \(CGPA\) reflects overall weighted performance across all completed semesters.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A minimum Cumulative Grade Point Average \(CGPA\) of 5.00 is strictly required for the award of degree.) Tj
0 -14 Td
